"""harnessblender: blend ingredients (skills + agents + richtlijnen + mcp servers) from a
cookbook into installable Claude Code plugins ("blends"), and pour them into projects.

Terminology:
  ingredients = pantry (your own skills/agents/richtlijnen/mcp-servers) + store
                (external sources, declared in store.yaml, cloned into store/<name>/ — gitignored)
  recipe      = a chosen selection of ingredients, saved in recipes/<naam>/recipe.yaml
  blend       = build a recipe into recipes/<naam>/blend/: real copies (no symlinks) + plugin.json +
                provenance, so a blend is self-contained and transferable
  cookbook    = the directory holding pantry/, store/, recipes/ — found by walking up from the
                current directory for a `cookbook.yaml` marker file (or --cookbook)
  pour        = install a blend into a "drinker" (a project folder) via the Claude Code CLI

harnessblender itself carries no personal content — everything specific lives in a cookbook.
"""
